# R4: the SSD-tier order through file modification times. The cleaner (nixl_cleaner.py) is not changed.
# Pseudo-diff against HEAD b7074d9cae; not applied. The retire half needs R3's marks and the prefetcher.
#
# Where a chain's file paths are known
#   page key   UnifiedTreeNode.hash_value: one hex SHA-256 per 64-token page of the node's key
#              (unified_tree_core.py:126; filled at _add_new_node :1484-1485 through
#              compute_node_hash_values, mem_cache/utils.py:172-181; at insert_host :2230 for pages read back;
#              sliced at _split_node :1424-1426). k_j = H(k_{j-1}, tokens of page j), seeded by the parent's
#              last hash (utils.py:148-158), so a key names the whole prefix up to its page.
#   file name  HiCacheNixl: <key>_<model>_<tp_rank>_<tp_size> (hicache_nixl.py:116-119, 191-192), then "_k" and
#              "_v" under the zero-copy layout (:666-675; campaigns 28-35: two 3 MiB files a page), one file
#              otherwise; path = <base dir>/<2 hex bucket>/<name> (nixl_utils.py:284-289,
#              nixl_routing.py:16-24). A pure function of the page key and the backend's config: the write
#              thread already computes it for touch_if_stored (hicache_nixl.py:853-875).
#   So: the tree (scheduler thread) knows the keys, the backend knows the paths. The scheduler thread hands
#   over key lists only; path building (one blake2b a file) and every utime run on the backend's own thread.
#
# Enumerating a chain
#   at a request   match_prefix returns last_host_node, the deepest node memory serves (GPU or host,
#                  unified_tree_core.py:989-995). The chain is that node and its ancestors; a partial match
#                  has already split the node (:881-886), so whole nodes only. Request matches carry
#                  params.req (schedule_batch.py:1624-1635): arrival (scheduler.py:3140), every admission pass
#                  (:4025) and the re-match after the prompt insert (unified_radix_cache.py:1378). The
#                  prefetcher's probes pass no req.
#   at the end     on_turn_committed gets tail_node_id (unified_radix_cache.py:1240), the node of the last
#                  pages inserted. The turn just ran, so its whole prompt is on the GPU and every node of the
#                  chain is in the tree. The session's own pages are those past its first prompt
#                  (campaign 34 trace: later sessions take 2.63 M tokens from other sessions' first prompts,
#                  1.86 M of them after the owner ended, and 0.027 M from other sessions' later turns).
#
# utime calls (campaign 34 ec_full, two files a page; out/client_stats_c34_ec_full.out)
#   retire   p50 678, p90 1,842, max 3,034 per ended session; 484 K in the run = 68/s
#   refresh  largest single request 1,920-2,032; mean 137/s at 900 s, 239/s at 300 s, 643/s at 60 s
#            (upper bounds: sessions counted as disjoint)
#   cost     1.1-1.6 us per os.utime on this host's ext4 with warm inodes (out/utime_bench.out, measured on
#            /dev/vda1; the SSD volume is ext4 too; a cold inode costs a metadata read, not measured)

--- a/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/hicache_storage.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/hicache_storage.py
@@ -346,3 +346,10 @@ class HiCacheStorage(ABC):
     def take_stored_write_skips(self) -> int:
         """Pages a set call found already stored and did not write, since the last call."""
         return 0
